 true] [17592186133935 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398022 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186152241 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397835 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186175951 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397877 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186176009 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397940 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186184154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397919 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186184154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397926 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186184154 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397933 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186192808 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397994 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186192808 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398001 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186192808 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398008 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198382 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397953 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198384 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397960 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198384 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397987 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198395 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397967 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198395 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397974 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198588 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194129 13194139533472 17592186045585 false] [17592186198588 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397947 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198588 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198588 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\ny=x,\\,y=3x,\\,y=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y=\\frac{5}{x}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}},\\,\\,),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198588 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n$y = x, y = 3x, y = \\frac{1}{x}, y = \\frac{5}{x}$.\n\nA transformation $T$, where\n\n$T: (u, v) → (x(u, v), y(u, v))$,\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n$T: (u, v) → (\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}, A A)$,\nwhat could be the missing expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 false] [17592186198588 1074 "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\ny=x,\\,y=3x,\\,y=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y=\\frac{5}{x}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}=1,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=3,\\,xy=1,\\,xy=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ and $v(x,y)=xy,$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{y}{x}\\,,\\,xy).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ v=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $y=ux.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $y=ux,$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny=u\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt{uv}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}},\\,\\sqrt{uv}).\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198616 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194297 13194139533472 17592186045585 false] [17592186198616 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397981 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198616 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198616 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x, y, z) = ⟨x^{2}, y^{2}, z^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z = x + y$ for $0 \\le x \\le 2$ and $0 \\le y \\le 2$. Using the parametrization $x = u$ and $y = v$, the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n$∬_(S)F \\cdot dS = \\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}AAAAAAAdvdu$.\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 false] [17592186198616 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186198616 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}+2uv+{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397787 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1069 "q-127736" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1071 "Calculate ${Z}^{-1}$ where\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1072 #uuid "9fd0e8ab-5ed1-5462-b099-07b3173547c9" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397786 1074 "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Z$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=1\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 2=2\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z{Z}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Z}^{-1}Z & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397788 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397789 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397790 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397791 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397792 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397792 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397787 1080 #uuid "16d27f97-4329-5b65-b357-06a7d75d56ef" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397788 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397788 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397788 1084 #uuid "bce01ee3-e62d-5dbf-8ab7-ab7ffd839257" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397789 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397789 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397789 1084 #uuid "cb1c7834-02fe-5c78-b2fe-aa883eb34976" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397790 1081 "\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397790 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397790 1084 #uuid "c2e1ebaa-2f3e-5015-b022-3d3df282249e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397791 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397791 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397791 1084 #uuid "717243f7-02ac-50c5-9655-63bba2b18b42" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397792 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397792 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397792 1084 #uuid "fcfc218d-9756-5117-a5b1-a400cbe24097" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397794 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1069 "q-127737" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1071 "Calculate ${U}^{-1}$, where \n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1072 #uuid "e9cf7ac8-28c7-510c-8205-256a03a04ef2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397793 1074 "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $U$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(U)=-2\\cdot 7-(-5)\\cdot 3=1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U{U}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {U}^{-1}U & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397795 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397796 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397797 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397798 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397799 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397798 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397794 1080 #uuid "194044ba-41ba-5420-975a-652d3ae5b598" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397795 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397795 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397795 1084 #uuid "ad7ce0b9-8bef-5a30-a632-26629274772f" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397796 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}