e] [17592186397953 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397954 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397953 1069 "q-161086" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397953 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397953 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\ny=2x,\\,y=5x,\\,y=\\frac{3}{x},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\,,\\,\\,\\sqrt{uv}),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397953 1072 #uuid "e82a0cbf-06e5-5031-a4c7-160ebc24fbd2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397953 1074 "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\ny=2x,\\,y=5x,\\,y=\\frac{3}{x},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}=2,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5,\\,xy=3,\\,xy=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ and $v(x,y)=xy,$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{y}{x}\\,,\\,xy).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ v=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $y=ux.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $y=ux,$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny=u\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt{uv}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}},\\,\\sqrt{uv}).\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397955 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397956 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397957 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397958 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397959 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397959 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1080 #uuid "a2f44abc-ac48-5c5f-840d-7b78fa1a5463" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1081 "\\sqrt{\\frac{{v}^{2}}{u}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1084 #uuid "2522b823-b6ab-5931-a981-d1897549cad3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1081 "\\frac{v}{u}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1084 #uuid "b6492003-1c71-5f35-931d-cbf5fe819f15" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1081 "\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1084 #uuid "f8c90f3c-320e-52bd-b987-c216a3f4625d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397958 1081 "\\frac{u}{v}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [175