c357f15c93a3eaad665e73b47a.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36\\,}.\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398010 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398011 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398012 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398013 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398014 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398012 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398009 1080 #uuid "634120e7-888a-527b-b321-8e6ce84d2f2c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398010 1081 "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398010 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398010 1084 #uuid "e217ad3d-748d-5af0-96b1-e1ce473458d5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398011 1081 "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}>36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398011 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398011 1084 #uuid "cd0bfd32-77d4-5a28-b13f-6b03980aac88" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398012 1081 "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398012 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398012 1084 #uuid "d591b7a8-1678-5fc4-8efb-59323697512e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398013 1081 "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398013 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398013 1084 #uuid "b121b495-13d7-5ac2-843d-1f8022ddb37d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398014 1081 "{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\ge 36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398014 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398014 1084 #uuid "b5797dbb-800e-55ff-b8bd-e000ab812acf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398016 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1069 "q-162581" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=1,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=xy\\,i+2y\\,j+{x}^{2}zk,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1072 #uuid "e0d14173-8029-50a6-8f00-d7853c057071" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398015 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z) \\\\  & =y+2+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+y+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}({x}^{2}+y+2)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,{x}^{2}+y+2\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398017 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398018 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398019 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398020 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398021 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398021 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398016 1080 #uuid "196954bd-17a6-525e-a3ea-36557f290435" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398017 1081 "2x+y+1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398017 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398017 1084 #uuid "0a60a0ff-d58d-574d-ad7b-aa68f48f45e3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398018 1081 "xy+2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398018 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398018 1084 #uuid "caf3aed4-56d3-57fb-9c54-0b9379ad0474" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398019 1081 "{x}^{2}+2y" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398019 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398019 1084 #uuid "5e393df8-940d-5225-8bcc-4aba9a085593" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398020 1081 "{x}^{2}+xy" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398020 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398020 1084 #uuid "8ebc6e76-bfea-5200-aea9-f978a3678ba3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398021 1081 "{x}^{2}+y+2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398021 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398021 1084 #uuid "c0a5acac-f897-54fc-9f0e-b6da562e322e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398023 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1069 "q-162583" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1071 "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=0,$ $x=4,$ $y=-1,$ $y=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=2.$ Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F=({x}^{2}+y)\\,i-yz\\,j+4xz\\,k,$ the flux of $F$ across $S$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1072 #uuid "20faa8ac-7475-55a0-94fb-35eb1571259e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398022 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4xz) \\\\  & =2x-z+4x \\\\  & =6x-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(6x-z)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,6x-z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398024 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398025 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398026 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398027 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398028 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398026 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398023 1080 #uuid "5b4c4f1b-ebdf-554c-9f5f-c8043f8e6124" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398024 1081 "2x+3z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398024 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398024 1084 #uuid "fc53f04c-d5bb-59dd-b389-8e0eefab0229" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398025 1081 "2x-z+4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398025 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398025 1084 #uuid "af12ea26-8299-5100-8312-7691bb7b67f0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398026 1081 "6x-z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398026 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398026 1084 #uuid "958be202-ad70-5f65-942d-3cf053018cf9" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398027 1081 "6x+4z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398027 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398027 1084 #uuid "221c39d4-97a7-58e1-af0f-bd5bd145ae18" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398028 1081 "2x-y-2z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398028 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398028 1084 #uuid "fc84079a-9c1c-54c9-bc3c-5fd874d6a1dc" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398030 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1069 "q-162644" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1071 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1072 #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398029 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398031 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398032 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398033 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398034 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398035 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398031 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398030 1080 #uuid "4112b8f8-a1d3-5ca1-a272-50f00bc81e5d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398031 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398031 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398031 1084 #uuid "bfa1654c-e948-5fc3-a89a-4fe52cc8fccf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398032 1081 "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398032 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398032 1084 #uuid "8d1b7514-50b8-5ddd-9dc3-5b90007cd7cf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398033 1081 "3\\pi n" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398033 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398033 1084 #uuid "61124a49-e750-5eed-9f63-4fab70f48c25" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398034 1081 "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398034 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398034 1084 #uuid "282a04d7-5121-553a-8c70-66602f8c83db" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398035 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398035 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398035 1084 #uuid "4a1c8270-8fd2-50fc-8447-30acc60e9312" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398037 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1069 "q-163839" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1071 "![](images/b9/b99ff5d9d55de34b2cb3e2176e7c4171a5583e1e010626796c3ca2f9d9ed29cb.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above.\nWhat is the global maximum of the function?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1072 #uuid "7c94f5db-a52d-5269-9d70-48b35e30ba08" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398036 1074 "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global maximum of a function is the largest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global maximum.\n\n- A global maximum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global maximum. There can be zero, one, or many global maximum points.\n\nFor our function, the maximum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=10.$ Therefore, the global maximum is $10.$ The function reaches this value at both $(x,y)=(2,4)$ and $(x,y)=(-4,4).$\n\n![](images/bf/bf82159ccb39f6c07fa870abe04911847dcbb240bd1cf5e6be8a1216fa9cf327.png)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398038 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398039 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398040 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398041 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398042 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398039 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398037 1080 #uuid "ea34e434-1d65-55e5-98c8-c4dc723100a6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398038 1081 "12" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398038 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398038 1084 #uuid "43d7fcb0-ff70-592c-ad54-21abfd7d0ab1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398039 1081 "10" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398039 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398039 1084 #uuid "b69485bc-fe91-5715-a1be-f3a4cae4eec7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398040 1081 "8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398040 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398040 1084 #uuid "0fd4e3aa-8ad0-50a4-8f3f-5869b4c7e1f2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398041 1081 "6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398041 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398041 1084 #uuid "5b5ce768-5